Tree: Tree is a non-linear and hierarchical data structure where each
node has child nodes.

Binary tree: A binary tree is a special tree where each node has
at most two children reffered to as left child and right child.

         12  - root node 
        / \
       89  45
       / \   \
      43  34  67 - leaf nodes
      
      Each node has three parts : data, lptr, rptr
 Parent Node: A node that id the direct ancestor of a node.
 Child Node: A Node that is direct descendent of another node.
 Edge: The link/connection between a parent node and child node.
 Leaf node: A node that doesn't have any children.
 Internal Node: A node that has atleast one child.
 Depth/level: The number of edges in the path from the root to
 that node. The depth/level of root node is 0.
 Hight: The number of edges on the longest path from root to a leaf.
 
 
 
 Properties:
 
 i)The maximum number of nodes at level L of a binary tree is 2^L.
 
 L=3   max nodes=2^3=8
 
 ii)The maximum number of nodes in a binary tree of height H is 
 2^(H+1) - 1
 
 H=4  max nodes=2^(4+1) - 1 =32 -1 =31
 
 iii)Total number of leaf nodes = Number of nodes with 2 children + 1
 
 
 Operations: 
 i)Traversal(visiting all nodes )
 
   a)DFS(Depth First Search Traversal) - Inorder, Preorder, Postorder
        
         12  - root node 
        / \
       89  45
       / \   \
      43  34  67 - leaf nodes
   Inorder : Left -> Root -> Right
   Preorder: Root -> Left -> Right
   PostOrder: Left ->Right -> Root
   
   43,89,34,12,45,67
   12,89,43,34,45,67
   43,34,89,67,45,12
   
   
   
   b)BFS(Breadth First Search Traversal)
   
     5
    / \
   12  13
   /   / \ 
   7  14  2
  / \ / \  
 17 2327 23
 
 [5]
 [12,13]
 [7,14,2]
 [17,23,27,23]
 
 

 
 ways:
 i)Recursive - O(n)
 ii)Iterative - O(n)
 
 
 ii)Searching
 iii)Insertion/Deleteion


Zigzag Traversal:(Spiral order)

This is a variation of level order traversal where the direction of 
traversal changes at every level.


     5
    / \
   12  13
   /   / \ 
   7   14  2
  / \  / \  
 17 23 27 23
 
 [5]
 [13,12]
 [7,14,2]
 [23,27,23,17]
 
 Balanced Trees:
 A binary tree is called a balanced binary tree if the height 
 difference between the left and the right subtree of every node
 is at most 1.


Condition: Height(Left)-Height(right)<=1

     5
    / \
   12  13
   /   / \ 
   7   14  2
  / \  / \  
 17 23 27 23
 
 left subtree height: 3
 
 right subtree height: 3
 
 difference=3-3=0
 Tree is balanced
 
 
            1
           /
		  2
		 /
		3 
	   /
	  4  	

 left subtree height: 3
 
 right subtree height: 0
 
 
difference=3-0=3

Not balanced.

Constructing tree from traversal:

i)Preorder+Inorder - possible
ii)Postorder+Inorder -possible
iii)Preorder+Postorder -- not unique








 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
  